{"surah": 99, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "إِذَا زُلْزِلَتِ ٱلْأَرْضُ زِلْزَالَهَا ", "translation": "When the earth is shaken with its [final] earthquake", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "زُلْزِلَتِ", "translit": "ِtَlِzْlُz", "root": "زلزل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضُ", "translit": "ُḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "زِلْزَالَهَا", "translit": "āَhَlāَzْlِz", "root": "زلزل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "وَأَخْرَجَتِ ٱلْأَرْضُ أَثْقَالَهَا ", "translation": "And the earth discharges its burdens[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَخْرَجَتِ", "translit": "ِtَjgَrْhkَaʾَw", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضُ", "translit": "ُḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَثْقَالَهَا", "translit": "āَhَlāَqْhtَaʾ", "root": "ثقل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَقَالَ ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ مَا لَهَا ", "translation": "And man says,[1] \"What is [wrong] with it?\" -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ", "translit": "ُnَٰsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَهَا", "translit": "āَhَl", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "يَوْمَئِذٍ تُحَدِّثُ أَخْبَارَهَا ", "translation": "That Day, it will report its news", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَوْمَئِذٍ", "translit": "ٍhdِyʾَmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تُحَدِّثُ", "translit": "ُhtِّdَḥُt", "root": "حدث"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَخْبَارَهَا", "translit": "āَhَrāَbْhkَaʾ", "root": "خبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "بِأَنَّ رَبَّكَ أَوْحَىٰ لَهَا ", "translation": "Because your Lord has inspired [i.e., commanded] it.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "بِأَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَوْحَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَḥْwَaʾ", "root": "وحي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَهَا", "translit": "āَhَl", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "يَوْمَئِذٍ يَصْدُرُ ٱلنَّاسُ أَشْتَاتًا لِّيُرَوْا۟ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ ", "translation": "That Day, the people will depart[1] separated [into categories] to be shown [the result of] their deeds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَوْمَئِذٍ", "translit": "ٍhdِyʾَmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَصْدُرُ", "translit": "ُrُdْṣَy", "root": "صدر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسُ", "translit": "ُsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَشْتَاتًا", "translit": "āًtāَtْhsَaʾ", "root": "شتت"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لِّيُرَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَrُyِّl", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَٰmْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "فَمَن يَعْمَلْ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ خَيْرًا يَرَهُۥ ", "translation": "So whoever does an atom's weight[1] of good will see it,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَمَن", "translit": "nَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَعْمَلْ", "translit": "ْlَmْʿعَy", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِثْقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqْhtِm", "root": "ثقل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ذَرَّةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَّrَhd", "root": "ذرر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "خَيْرًا", "translit": "āًrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَرَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَrَy", "root": "راي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "وَمَن يَعْمَلْ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ شَرًّا يَرَهُۥ ", "translation": "And whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَعْمَلْ", "translit": "ْlَmْʿعَy", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِثْقَالَ", "translit": "َlāَqْhtِm", "root": "ثقل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ذَرَّةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَّrَhd", "root": "ذرر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "شَرًّا", "translit": "āًّrَhs", "root": "شرر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَرَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَrَy", "root": "راي"}], "hasIhya": true}], "tafsir": {"6": [{"arabic": "وقال تعالى يومئذ يصدر الناس أشتاتا ليروا أعمالهم فمن يعمل مثقال ذرة خيرا يره ومن يعمل مثقال ذرة شرا يره وقال تعالى ثم توفى كل نفس ما كسبت وهم لا يظلمون وقال تعالى يوم تجد كل نفس ما عملت من خير محضرا وما عملت من سوء تود لو أن بينها وبينه أمدا بعيدا ويحذركم الله نفسه وقال تعالى واعلموا أن الله يعلم ما في أنفسكم فاحذروه فعرف أرباب البصائر من جملة العباد أن الله تعالى لهم بالمرصاد وأنهم سيناقشون في الحساب ويطالبون بمثاقيل الذر من الخطرات واللحظات وتحققوا أنه لا ينجيهم من هذه الأخطار إلا لزوم المحاسب", "english": "And He (Exalted) said: 'On that day, the people will emerge in scattered groups to be shown their deeds. So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.' And He (Exalted) said: 'Then every soul (Nafs) will be fully compensated for what it earned, and they will not be wronged.' And He (Exalted) said: 'On the day when every soul (Nafs) will find what it did of good present [before it], and what it did of evil, it will wish that between it and that [evil] was a great distance. And Allah warns you of Himself.' And He (Exalted) said: 'And know that Allah knows what is in your souls (Anfus), so beware of Him.' So the possessors of insight (Arbab al-Basa'ir) from among the servants recognized that Allah (Exalted) is lying in wait for them, and that they will be scrutinized in the accounting and held accountable for atom's weights of thoughts (Khatarat) and glances (Lahazat). And they realized that nothing will save them from these dangers except adhering to self-accounting (Muhasabah) and sincere self-observation (Muraqabah), and demanding from the soul (Nafs) in breaths (Anfas) and movements (Harakat), and accounting it for thoughts (Khatarat) and glances (Lahazat). For whoever accounts his soul (Nafs) before being accounted for, his accounting on the Day of Resurrection (Qiyamah) will be lightened, and his answer will be present at the questioning, and his return and outcome will be good. And whoever does not account his soul (Nafs), his regrets will persist, and his pauses in the gathering places of the Day of Resurrection (Qiyamah) will be prolonged, and his evil deeds will lead him to disgrace and contempt.", "book_file": "vol4_j4-k08.doc.txt", "book_title": "Monitoring and Accounting", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Monitoring and Accounting'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "فاستعد يا مسكين لهذا اليوم العظيم شأنه المديد زمانه القاهر سلطانه القريب أوانه، يوم ترى السماء فيه قد انفطرت، والكواكب من هوله قد انتثرت، والنجوم الزواهر قد انكدرت، والشمس قد كورت، والجبال قد سيرت، والعشار قد عطلت، والوحوش قد حشرت، والبحار قد سجرت والنفوس إلى الأبدان قد زوجت، والجحيم قد سعرت، والجنة قد أزلفت، والجبال قد نسفت، والأرض قد مدت، يوم ترى الأرض قد زلزلت فيه زالزالها، وأخرجت الأرض أثقالها، يومئذ يصدر الناس أشتاتا ليروا أعمالهم، يوم تحمل الأرض والجبال فدكتا دكة واحدة، فيومئذ وقعت الواقعة", "english": "Prepare, O wretched one, for this day of great affair, long in its time, overpowering in its dominion, near in its occurrence, a day when you will see the sky therein has split, and the planets from its terror have scattered, and the shining stars have been extinguished, and the sun has been rolled up, and the mountains have been set in motion, and the pregnant camels have been neglected, and the wild beasts have been gathered, and the seas have been set ablaze, and the souls (Nafs) to the bodies have been paired, and Hell has been kindled, and Paradise has been brought near, and the mountains have been blown away, and the earth has been stretched out, a day when you will see the earth has quaked with its quaking, and the earth has brought forth its burdens, on that day the people will issue forth in scattered groups to be shown their deeds, a day when the earth and the mountains will be lifted and crushed with a single crushing, and then the Inevitable Event will occur and the sky will be split, so it is on that day frail, and the angels are at its edges, and the Throne of your Lord will be carried above them on that day by eight, on that day you will be presented, nothing of you will be hidden, a day when the mountains will move and you will see the earth bare, a day when the earth will be shaken with its shaking and the mountains will be pulverized with pulverization so they become scattered dust, a day when the people will be like scattered moths and the mountains will be like carded wool, a day when every nursing mother will be distracted from what she nursed and every pregnant one will deliver her burden and you will see the people intoxicated yet they are not intoxicated but the punishment of Allah is severe, a day when the earth will be changed to other than the earth and the heavens and they will appear before Allah the One, the Subduer, a day when the mountains will be blown away with blowing so they leave a level plain, you will see in it no crookedness nor unevenness, a day when you will see the mountains, you think them fixed while they pass like the passing of clouds, a day when the sky will be split so it becomes like red leather, and on that day no human or jinn will be asked about his sin, a day when the disobedient will be prevented from speech and in it there will be no inquiry about crimes but they will be seized by the forelocks and the feet, a day when every soul (Nafs) will find what it did of good present and what it did of evil it wishes that between it and it were a distant span, a day when every soul (Nafs) will know what it has brought and will witness what it sent ahead and left behind, a day when the tongues will be silenced and the limbs will speak, a day whose mention has turned gray, O master of the...", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on death, the grave, and preparation for the Hereafter, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "7": [{"arabic": "فإذا طاب شراب الأبرار لشوب الشراب الصرف الذي هو للمقربين. والشراب عبارة عن جملة نعيم الجنان، كما أن الكتاب عبر به عن جميع الأعمال فقال: \"إن كتاب الأبرار لفي عليين\" ثم قال: \"يشهده المقربون\" فكان أمارة علة كتابهم أنه ارتفع إلى حيث يشهده المقربون، وكما أن الأبرار يجدون المزيد في حالهم ومعرفتهم بقربهم من المقربين ومشاهدتهم لهم، فكذلك يكون حالهم في الآخرة \"ما خلقكم ولا بعثكم إلا كنفس واحدة كما بدأنا أول خلق نعيده\"، وكما قال تعالى: \"جزاء وفاقاً\" أي وافق الجزاء أعمالهم فقوبل الخالص بالصرف من الشراب وقو", "english": "So if the drink of the righteous becomes pleasant due to the mixing of the pure drink which is for the close ones. And the drink is an expression for the entirety of the bliss of the Gardens, just as the Book expressed by it all the deeds saying: \"Indeed, the record of the righteous is in 'Illiyyun\" then said: \"Witnessed by those brought near\" so it was a sign of the reason for their record that it rose to where those brought near witness it, and just as the righteous find increase in their state and knowledge by their closeness to those brought near and their witnessing of them, so will be their state in the Hereafter \"He did not create you nor resurrect you except as a single soul as We began the first creation We will repeat it\", and as Allah the Exalted said: \"A reward matching\" meaning the reward corresponded to their deeds, so the pure was met with the pure from the drink and the mixed was met with the mixed, and the mixing of every drink is according to what preceded of mixing in his love and his deeds \"So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it - and Allah does not change what is in a people until they change what is in their souls - Indeed, Allah does not do injustice, [even] as much as an atom's weight; and if there is a good deed, He multiplies it - and if it is the weight of a mustard seed, We will bring it forth, and sufficient are We as accountant\" So whoever his love in the world was his hope for the bliss of the Garden and the wide-eyed maidens and palaces, he is enabled in the Garden to settle wherever he wishes to play with the eternal youths and enjoy the women; there his pleasure ends in the Hereafter because indeed every human is given in love what his soul (Nafs) desires and his eye delights in.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book6.doc.txt", "book_title": "Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "اعلم أن العمل إذا لم يكن خالصا لوجه الله تعالى بل امتزج به شوب من الرياء أو حظوظ النفس فقد اختلف الناس في أن ذلك هل يقتضي ثوابا أم يقتضي عقابا أم لا يقتضي شيئا أصلا فلا يكون له ولا عليه أما الذي لم يرد به إلا الرياء فهو عليه قطعا وهو سبب المقت والعقاب وأما الخالص لوجه الله تعالى فهو سبب الثواب وإنما النظر في المشوب وظاهر الأخبار تدل على أنه لا ثواب له[45] وليس تخلو الأخبار عن تعارض فيه والذي ينقدح لما فيه والعلم عند الله أن ينظر إلى قدر قوة الباعث فإن كان الباعث الديني مساويا للباعث النفسي تقاوم", "english": "Know that if the deed is not purely for the Face (Wajh) of Allah the Exalted, but rather mixed with a taint of showing off (Riya') or desires of the Soul (Nafs), then people have differed regarding whether that necessitates reward or necessitates punishment or necessitates nothing at all, so it is neither for him nor against him. As for that which was intended only with showing off (Riya'), it is against him decisively and is a cause of wrath and punishment. And as for that which is purely for the Face (Wajh) of Allah the Exalted, it is a cause of reward. The consideration is regarding the mixed [deed]. The apparent reports indicate that there is no reward for it, and the reports are not free from contradiction in this matter. What becomes clear regarding it—and knowledge is with Allah—is to look at the measure of the strength of the motivator. If the religious motivator is equal to the soul (Nafs) motivator, they counterbalance and cancel each other out, and the deed becomes neither for him nor against him. And if the motivator of showing off (Riya') is predominant and stronger, then it is not beneficial, and it is moreover harmful and leads to punishment—yes, the punishment in it is lighter than the punishment of the deed that was purely for showing off (Riya') and not mixed with any taint of drawing near (Taqarrub). And if the intention of drawing near (Taqarrub) is predominant in comparison to the other motivator, then he has reward according to what remains of the strength of the religious motivator. And this is due to His saying, the Exalted: 'So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it' (Quran 99:7-8), and due to His saying, the Exalted: 'Indeed, Allah does not do injustice, [even] as much as an atom's weight; and if there is a good deed, He multiplies it' (Quran 4:40). So it is not fitting that the intention of good be wasted. Rather, if it is predominant over the intention of showing off (Riya'), the amount that equals it is invalidated, and the increase remains. And if it is overcome, something of the punishment of the corrupt intention falls away because of it.", "book_file": "vol4_j4-k07-old.doc.txt", "book_title": "Intention, Sincerity and Truthfulness", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's insights on the inner dimensions of faith, from 'Intention, Sincerity and Truthfulness'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "والفضيلة نسبية واستحقارنا للصيارفة عند قياسهم بالملوك لا يدل على حقارتهم إذا قيسوا بالكناسين فلا تظن أن ما نزل عن الرتبة القصوى ساقط القدر بل الرتبة العليا للأنبياء ثم الأولياء ثم العلماء الراسخين في العلم ثم للصالحين على تفاوت درجاتهم وبالجملة فمن يعمل مثقال ذرة خيرا يره ومن يعمل مثقال ذرة شرا يره ومن قصد الله تعالى بالعلم أي علم كان نفعه ورفعه لا محالة.", "english": "And virtue is relative, and our belittling of money-changers when comparing them to kings does not indicate their lowliness when compared to sweepers. So do not think that what falls below the highest rank is of diminished worth, but rather the highest rank is for the Prophets, then the Friends (Awliya), then the firmly-grounded scholars in knowledge, then for the righteous with varying degrees among them. And in summary: 'So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it' (Quran 99:7-8). And whoever intends Allah the Exalted with knowledge, whatever knowledge it may be, his benefit and elevation are inevitable.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-1.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the diseases of the heart and their cure, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Ethics"}, {"arabic": "فأما إذا كان بحيث لولا الناس أيضاً لكان يصلي إلا أنه ظهر له الرغبة في المحمدة أيضاً فاجتمع الباعثان، فهذا إما أن يكون في صدقة وقراءة وما ليس فيه تحليل وتحريم أو في عقد صلاة وحج، فإن كان في صدقة فقد عصى بإجابة باعث الرياء وأطاع بإجابة باعث الثواب \"فمن يعمل مثقال ذرة خيراً يره ومن يعمل مثقال ذرة شراً يره\" فله ثواب بقدر قصده الصحيح وعقاب بقدر قصده الفاسد ولا يحبط أحدهما الآخر.", "english": "As for if he was such that even without people he would still pray, except that the desire for praise also appeared to him, so the two motivators combined - this is either in charity and recitation and what does not involve permissibility and prohibition, or in the contract of prayer and pilgrimage. If it was in charity, then he has disobeyed by responding to the motivator of showing off (Riya') and obeyed by responding to the motivator of reward. \"So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.\" So for him is reward according to the measure of his correct intention (Qasd) and punishment according to the measure of his corrupt intention, and one does not nullify the other.", "book_file": "vol3_Vol3-book-8a.doc.txt", "book_title": "Condemnation of Status and Ostentation", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications and their spiritual significance, from 'Condemnation of Status and Ostentation'", "badge": "Du'a"}, {"arabic": "حديث الرجل الذي جاء ليتعلم فانتهى إلى قوله تعالى فمن يعمل مثقال ذرة خيرا يره ومن يعمل مثقال ذرة شرا يره فقال يكفني هذا وانصرف فقال النبي ﷺ انصرف الرجل وهو فقيه أخرجه أبو داود والنسائي في الكبرى وابن حبان والحاكم وصححه من حديث عبد الله بن عمرو قال أتى رجل رسول الله ﷺ فقال أقرئني يا رسول الله الحديث وفيه فأقرأه رسول الله ﷺ إذا زلزلت حتى فرغ منها فقال الرجل والذي بعثك بالحق لا أزيد عليهما أبدا ثم أدبر الرجل فقال رسول الله ﷺ أفلح الرويجل أفلح الرويجل ولأحمد والنسائي في الكبرى من حديث صعصعة عم الفرزد", "english": "The narration of the man who came to learn and reached the saying of Allah the Exalted: 'So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.' He said: 'This is sufficient for me,' and departed. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'The man departed as a jurist (faqih).' Reported by Abu Dawud, al-Nasa'i in al-Kubra, Ibn Hibban, and al-Hakim who authenticated it from the narration of Abdullah ibn Amr who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: 'Recite to me, O Messenger of Allah...' In it: So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) recited to him 'When the earth is shaken' until he finished it. The man said: 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never add to these two.' Then the man turned away. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'The man has succeeded, the man has succeeded.' And for Ahmad and al-Nasa'i in al-Kubra from the narration of Sa'sa'ah, the uncle of al-Farazdaq, that he was the companion of the verse (an-nassah) and said: 'It is enough for me, I do not care to hear other than it.'", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-8.doc.txt", "book_title": "Etiquette of Quran Recitation", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions cited by Al-Ghazali with scholarly authentication, from 'Etiquette of Quran Recitation'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "8": [{"arabic": "ومن ذلك أن يغلب على قلبه أن (من يعمل مثقال ذرة خيرا يرهُ  (  ومن  يعمل  مثقال ذرة شرا يره( (الزلزة: 8،7) وهو اليقين بالثواب والعقاب حتى يرى  نسبة  الطاعات إلى الثواب كنسبة الخبز إلى الشبع  ونسبة  المعاصي  إلى  العقاب  كنسبة  السموم والأفاعي إلى الهلاك فكما يحرص على  التحصيل  للخبز  طلبا  للشبع  فيحفظ  قليله وكثيره فكذلك يحرص على الطاعات كلها قليلها وكثيرها  وكما  يجتنب  قليل  السموم وكثيرها فكذلك يجتنب المعاصي قليلها وكثيرها وصغيرها وكبيرها  فاليقين  بالمعنى الأول قد يوجد لعموم المؤمنين أما بالم", "english": "And from that is that there overcomes upon his Heart (Qalb) that 'Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it' (Az-Zalzalah: 7-8). And it is the Certainty (Yaqeen) in reward and punishment until he sees the proportion of acts of obedience to reward like the proportion of bread to satiety, and the proportion of sins to punishment like the proportion of poisons and snakes to destruction. So just as he is eager for the acquisition of bread seeking satiety, and thus preserves its little and its much, likewise he is eager for all acts of obedience, their little and their much. And just as he avoids little poisons and their much, likewise he avoids sins, their little and their much, their small and their great. So the Certainty (Yaqeen) in the first meaning may exist for the generality of the believers, but as for the second meaning, it is specific to those brought near. And the fruit of this Certainty (Yaqeen) is the sincerity of self-observation (Muraqabah) in movements and stillness, in passing thoughts, and the utmost in God-consciousness (Taqwa) and guarding against every evil. And whenever the Certainty (Yaqeen) is more dominant, the guarding is more severe and the exertion is more complete.", "book_file": "vol1_Vol1-book-1.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "content_type": "dhikr", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the virtue and practice of remembering God, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Dhikr"}, {"arabic": "وليس من أمله مقصور على شهر كمن أمله شهر ويوم بل بينهما تفاوت في الدرجة عند الله فإن الله لا يظلم مثقال ذرة ﴿ وَمَنْ يَعْمَلْ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ خَيْرًا يَرَهُ ﴾ {} ثم يظهر أثر قصر الأمل في المبادرة إلى العمل وكل إنسان يدعى أنه قصير الأمل وهو كاذب، إنما يظهر ذلك بأعماله.", "english": "And it is not that his hope is limited to a month like one whose hope is for a month and a day, but between them there is a difference in degree with Allah, for Allah does not wrong (even) the weight of an atom (mithqāla dharratin). 'And whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it' (Quran 99:8). Then the effect of shortening hope appears in hastening to work, and every person claims that he has short hope, but he is lying; it only appears through his deeds.", "book_file": "vol4_Vol4-book10.doc.txt", "book_title": "Book of Repentance", "content_type": "general", "topic": "Commentary from Al-Ghazali's Ihya 'Ulum al-Din, from 'Book of Repentance'", "badge": "General"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 350, 1119], [2, 1119, 2105], [3, 2105, 3052], [4, 3052, 4651]], "2": [[1, 350, 1605], [2, 1605, 2491], [3, 2491, 4077]], "3": [[1, 350, 1602], [2, 1602, 3081], [3, 3081, 3695], [4, 3695, 4521]], "4": [[1, 350, 1888], [2, 1888, 3078], [3, 3078, 5096]], "5": [[1, 350, 1415], [2, 1415, 2274], [3, 2274, 3694], [4, 3694, 4495]], "6": [[1, 400, 1687], [2, 1687, 2652], [3, 2652, 3949], [4, 3949, 5477], [5, 5477, 6955], [6, 6955, 8344]], "7": [[1, 350, 1140], [2, 1140, 2378], [3, 2378, 3932], [4, 3932, 4893], [5, 4893, 6263], [6, 6263, 7159]], "8": [[1, 400, 1350], [2, 1350, 2626], [3, 2626, 4228], [4, 4228, 5219], [5, 5219, 6454], [6, 6454, 7377]]}, "husary": {"1": [[1, 400, 1765], [2, 1765, 3515], [3, 3515, 5195], [4, 5195, 8028]], "2": [[1, 350, 26